        "code": {
          "text": "Itchy rash"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports an itchy rash for approximately 3–4 weeks, worse at night, initially on the wrists and hands and now between the fingers, around the waistline/lower abdomen, and on the inner thighs."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Skin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Papules and excoriations on the wrists, interdigital spaces, lateral fingers, periumbilical/waistband area, inner thighs, and anterior axillary folds. A few linear burrows between the fingers. Small superficial pustules and crusting on the shins and forearms. Lesions non-tender, with no significant surrounding cellulitis. No features of crusted scabies."
      }
    },
